VTID-04283 — commands run to build and verify this change

1. User reported live (urgent): "why does it still show 30 new findings
   since so many hours. not one single of the new findings has started to
   be processed." Screenshot of Command Hub Autopilot Runs page.

2. Queried live production `autopilot_recommendations` for the current
   `source_type='dev_autopilot' status='new'` rows (via Supabase MCP
   execute_sql, read-only): 9 rows, all `[rollup]` findings from the
   already-flagged stuck run `cf77d23c` (2026-09-21). Confirmed
   `raw.affected_files`/`spec_snapshot.affected_files` DOES carry real
   per-file data (19-726 files depending on the finding) — ruled out the
   initial hypothesis that ROLLUP_EXEMPT_TYPES needed widening; the data
   was never missing.

3. Queried `dev_autopilot_plan_versions` for those 9 finding ids: only 3
   had ever been planned (one of them, `efec84e4`, is the same finding
   already fixed by VTID-04279's PR, replanned same-day after the fix).
   6 had zero plan versions; of those, 2 are `large_file`/risk_class=high
   (correctly excluded from lazy planning by design) and 4 are
   low/medium risk (dead_code, stale_flag, missing_tests, todo) and
   should have been lazy-planned.

4. Queried `self_healing_log` for those 4 findings' `VTID-DA-FIND-*` keys:
   zero rows — never even attempted, not failing-and-backing-off.

5. Read `lazyPlanTick()` in full
   (services/gateway/src/services/dev-autopilot-execute.ts). Confirmed it
   is scheduled every 30s via `startBackgroundExecutor()`
   (services/gateway/src/index.ts:1796-1798), gated only on
   `DEV_AUTOPILOT_EXECUTOR_ENABLED !== 'false'`.

6. Queried `dev_autopilot_worker_queue` for stuck kind=plan
   pending/running rows (the tick's own global guard) — none found, ruling
   out that as the blocker.

7. Queried the live impact-ranked candidate set directly:
   ```sql
   select ar.id, ar.source_type, ar.risk_class, ar.impact_score,
     (select count(*) from dev_autopilot_plan_versions pv
      where pv.finding_id=ar.id) as n_plans
   from autopilot_recommendations ar
   where ar.status='new' and ar.risk_class in ('low','medium')
   order by ar.impact_score desc, ar.created_at asc
   limit 30;
   ```
   Found 25+ `operator_onramp` findings (impact_score=5, created
   2026-09-13..2026-09-18, ALL already with n_plans=1) filling the entire
   top of the ranking. Confirmed `operator_onramp` is in
   `executableSourceTypesPostgrestIn()`'s allowlist, so it's a real
   candidate for `lazyPlanTick`'s query.

8. Root cause confirmed by reading the exact query
   (`limit=${LAZY_PLAN_BATCH_SIZE * 4}` = 12) and the loop body: it
   checked "does a plan exist?" ONE ROW AT A TIME via a per-candidate
   `dev_autopilot_plan_versions` query, `continue`-ing past planned rows.
   With 25+ already-planned rows ranked ahead of the 4 real candidates,
   every one of the 12 fetched rows on every tick was already-planned —
   `generated` stayed 0 forever, confirmed by the live evidence in steps
   3-4.

9. Fix: services/gateway/src/services/dev-autopilot-execute.ts —
   - New constants LAZY_PLAN_CANDIDATE_LIMIT (200, env-tunable via
     DEV_AUTOPILOT_LAZY_PLAN_CANDIDATE_LIMIT) and PLAN_CHECK_CHUNK_SIZE
     (60).
   - Candidate query limit raised from `LAZY_PLAN_BATCH_SIZE * 4` (12) to
     LAZY_PLAN_CANDIDATE_LIMIT (200).
   - New batch step: chunk candidateIds into groups of <=60, one
     `dev_autopilot_plan_versions?finding_id=in.(...)` query per chunk,
     union into a `plannedIds` Set. Fails open per chunk (a failed chunk's
     candidates fall through, not dropped).
   - `unplannedFindings = findingsR.data.filter(f => !plannedIds.has(f.id))`
     computed once, before the loop.
   - The loop below now iterates `unplannedFindings` and the old per-row
     `dev_autopilot_plan_versions` existence check inside it was removed
     (now redundant — done in batch above). The inflight-queue check and
     `planRetryDecision` backoff/exhaustion check are unchanged.

